  "text": "Your job is to design the most addictive slot machine. Here's how you do it. First, when a player loses, make sure it's a near miss. Studies show that the human brain reacts to near misses similarly to wins. It feels frustrating, but it pushes us to keep playing. Second, disguise losses as wins. If they bet a dollar and hit a 0.5 multiplier, they didn't just lose 50 cents, they won 50 cents. Celebrate it. Lights, sounds, animations. Now losing feels like winning. Lastly, make it fast. This is not a roulette where you wait ages between spins. Pack in as many spins per minute as possible. So they make so many plays, they enter into a betting-induced trance. Congrats, you just designed the most profitable casino game in history."
